    <string name="tut_rot_1_title">The Matrix</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_1_body">Your Phone (3) has a 489-LED display on the back. This app uses it to show your own GIFs every time you lock or unlock the phone.\n\nTurn the phone over to see it.</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_2_title">Your designs</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_2_body">Add whatever GIFs or images you want in the DESIGNS tab. They are copied into the app, so you can delete the originals safely.\n\nEach one is processed to read well at 25x25 dots: if one comes out wrong, tap it and try another render mode.</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_3_title">Turn it on</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_3_body">The main switch lives in STATUS. With it on, the Matrix cycles through your designs on its own.\n\nAndroid will ask for a permission or two the first time. They keep the service alive while the screen is off.</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_4_title">Clock and battery</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_4_body">In WHAT SHOWS you pick what appears at rest: the clock, the spinning record while music plays, the battery liquid when you plug the cable in.\n\nIn BATTERY you set the levels where it dims or switches itself off.</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_5_title">If you see nothing</string>
    <string name="tut_rot_5_body">The phone switches the Matrix off when it detects the screen facing up: turn it over.\n\nAnd if another Glyph app is open, this one steps aside rather than fighting it for the display.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_1_title">The game</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_1_body">Wild Pokémon appear on the Matrix while you are NOT using the phone. The longer you go without looking, the likelier one shows up.\n\nAfter an hour of screen-off time, an encounter is guaranteed.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_2_title">Catching</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_2_body">When one appears, press and hold the Glyph button on the back to catch it.\n\nFor the button to reach this app, its toy has to be the one selected in the system\'s Glyph settings.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_3_title">Training</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_3_body">Pick a buddy in TEAM and it gains experience for every minute the screen is off. It evolves on its own when it levels up, and you will see it on the Matrix.\n\nIn SETTINGS you can have it show up on a Glyph button press.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_4_title">Real life</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_4_body">Sleeping well, drinking water and keeping your habits multiply the experience your buddy earns. Breaking them genuinely slows it down.\n\nAdd your habits in MY HABITS and your water goal in WATER AND BONUS.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_5_title">Eggs</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_5_body">Every ten catches earns you an egg. They incubate while the phone rests, just like training.\n\nAn egg hatches into a base form, favouring the ones missing from your Pokédex.</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_6_title">Tracking</string>
    <string name="tut_pok_6_body">STATS has the calendar for each thing, and ACHIEVEMENTS shows what you have and what is left.\n\nIf you want to try everything fast, GAME has BALANCE AND DEMO MODE with the game\'s numbers and a switch that speeds it all up.</string>

